Clean build, no warnings, all tests pass. Here's a summary of the work.

## Changes

**`src/lib.rs`** — Added the public function:

```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```

Exact match via `==` on each tag (not substring), preserves relative order, returns references (no allocation of notes).

**`src/main.rs`** — Wired `--tag <TAG>` into the `list` command:
- Added a `list_tag` helper that parses the flag from `args[2..]`, returning `Option<String>`.
- The `list` arm now calls `filter_by_tag(&notes, &t)` when `--tag` is given, otherwise lists all.
- Errors out (exit 1) on a missing argument (`--tag` with no value) or unknown trailing args.

## Verification

- `cargo build` — clean, zero warnings.
- `cargo test` — 2/2 existing tests pass (existing behavior preserved).
- Functional end-to-end test with 4 notes:
  - `list --tag work` → returns the 2 notes tagged `work` (incl. one also tagged `travel`), order preserved.
  - `list --tag home` → returns the 2 `home` notes.
  - `list --tag travel` → returns the single `travel` note.
  - `list --tag nope` → empty output, exit 0.
  - `list --tag` (no value) → `--tag requires an argument`, exit 1.
  - `list --tag work extra` → `unknown list argument: extra`, exit 1.
  - `list` (no flag) → unchanged, all notes.

No source fixture or benchmark repository was touched; all work stayed under the disposable run root.


